<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<manifest xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    xmlns:tools="http://schemas.android.com/tools">

    <!--
      PRIVACY-CRITICAL FILE. See docs/TIMEOS_ENGINEERING_SPEC.md §8.2, §8.4, §26, §35.

      Phase 1A added PACKAGE_USAGE_STATS, which must be present in the manifest for the OS to
      list this app under Settings > Usage Access, even though it is granted via AppOpsManager
      rather than a runtime dialog. Phase 1B added RECEIVE_BOOT_COMPLETED so collection resumes
      promptly after a reboot (§8.4 mitigation). Phase 2 adds INTERNET — the sync client's whole
      purpose is uploading batches (§26) — which is the first phase this is legitimate; Phase
      1A/1B's manifest deliberately had no INTERNET at all, and ManifestPrivacyTest.kt enforced
      that as proof nothing left the device before now.

      This manifest still does NOT declare, and ManifestPrivacyTest.kt still enforces at build
      time, the actual privacy-sensitive permissions this system never touches:
        READ_CONTACTS, READ_SMS           - never collected, ever
        READ_PHONE_STATE, READ_PHONE_NUMBERS, READ_PRIVILEGED_PHONE_STATE - no hardware/SIM
                                             identifiers; device identity is a generated UUID
        BIND_NOTIFICATION_LISTENER_SERVICE - notification content deliberately excluded (§8.6)
        BIND_ACCESSIBILITY_SERVICE        - would expose window titles/text content; prohibited
        ACCESS_FINE_LOCATION / COARSE     - not part of this system
        CAMERA, RECORD_AUDIO              - not part of this system

      usesCleartextTraffic stays "false" here (production/release): TLS is mandatory per §28.
      A debug-only override (src/debug/AndroidManifest.xml + network_security_config_debug.xml)
      permits cleartext HTTP to 127.0.0.1 alone, for testing against the local mock server in
      tools/mock_ingest_server.py via `adb reverse` — never to any other host, and never in a
      release build.
    -->

    <uses-permission
        android:name="android.permission.PACKAGE_USAGE_STATS"
        tools:ignore="ProtectedPermissions" />
    <uses-permission android:name="android.permission.RECEIVE_BOOT_COMPLETED" />
    <uses-permission android:name="android.permission.INTERNET" />

    <application
        android:name=".TimeOSApplication"
        android:allowBackup="false"
        android:label="@string/app_name"
        android:icon="@mipmap/ic_launcher"
        android:theme="@style/Theme.TimeOS"
        android:usesCleartextTraffic="false">

        <activity
            android:name=".MainActivity"
            android:exported="true"
            android:theme="@style/Theme.TimeOS">
            <intent-filter>
                <action android:name="android.intent.action.MAIN" />
                <category android:name="android.intent.category.LAUNCHER" />
            </intent-filter>
        </activity>

        <receiver
            android:name=".BootReceiver"
            android:exported="false">
            <intent-filter>
                <action android:name="android.intent.action.BOOT_COMPLETED" />
            </intent-filter>
        </receiver>
    </application>
</manifest>
